  "score_support": "supports_wrong_score",
  "score_support_basis": "The rationale concludes the comment deserves a score of 5, which contradicts the correct gold label of 3, and contains multiple material errors in reasoning that lead to this incorrect score.",
  "error_sentences": [
    {
      "sentence": "The comment begins with \"2.)\", which likely refers to a specific section or point in the paper, making it fully grounded.",
      "error_type": "evidence_misread",
      "explanation": "The \"2.)\" is the numbering of the comment itself, not a reference to a specific section within the evaluated paper. The rationale incorrectly interprets this numbering as a reference to a part of the paper, distorting the evidence from the evaluated text."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The authors can confidently identify the part being addressed.",
      "error_type": "factual_error",
      "explanation": "This claim is incorrect because the comment does not specify which section, table, figure, or part of the paper the issue is in, so authors cannot confidently identify the part being addressed, which aligns with the gold label of 3 that states authors cannot confidently determine the part."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Therefore, the comment is fully grounded and specific, aligning with score 5.",
      "error_type": "rubric_misapplication",
      "explanation": "Per the scoring rubric, a score of 5 requires the comment to explicitly mention which part of the paper it addresses. This comment does not identify a specific part of the paper, only specifies what the issue is, so it does not meet the criteria for score 5. The rationale incorrectly applies the rubric threshold."
    }
  ],
  "overall_basis": "The rationale consistently supports an incorrect score of 5 through misinterpretation of the evaluated text and incorrect application of the scoring rubric, so it primarily supports the wrong score."
}
